# What `docker build` must NOT carry into the image.  INSTALL-SPEC.md §4 and §11.2.
#
# Two separate jobs, and only one of them is about size:
#
#  1. ⚠ **`*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` must not enter the context.** Route tests are
#     colocated with routes (the Next convention) and nothing imports them, so they are
#     never traced into `.next/standalone` — but `next build` type-checks everything
#     `tsconfig.json`'s `include` matches, and every one of those files imports `vitest`.
#     Excluding them means the type-check inside the image covers exactly the code that
#     ships. (INSTALL-SPEC §4: "Excluding them settles both.")
#  2. ⚠ **Nothing that carries a credential may be in a build context**, ever. A context is
#     uploaded to the daemon and every ADD/COPY layer is readable in the finished image.
#     `.env*` is listed here as well as in the repo's .gitignore for that reason.
#
# Everything else here is either regenerated inside the image (`node_modules`, `.next`) or
# is host-side material the container has no use for (`dashboard.sh`, `scripts/`,
# `systemd/`, `pipeline/`).
#
# ⚠ Docker matches these against paths relative to the context root, with Go's
# `filepath.Match` semantics — so a bare `node_modules` matches ONLY the root one. The
# `**/` twins below are not decoration.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated, never shipped
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.gitignore

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
# There should never be one of these here. If there ever is, it stops at this line.
#
# ⚠ The `**/` twins are MORE necessary here than anywhere else in this file, and until
# 2026-09-10 this was the one section that did not have them (11-A15): the note at the top
# explains that a bare `node_modules` matches only the root one, twins every generated
# pattern and every test pattern, and then left the section it calls "the one that must never
# be violated" root-only. `app/.env.local`, `lib/.env` and `components/deploy.apikey` would
# have gone to the daemon and into the build cache on the box. Nothing like that exists
# today, which is exactly when to write the twin.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*.apikey
**/*.apikey

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- tests
# See note 1 above. `test-support.ts`, `fixtures.ts` and `fake-env.ts` are deliberately NOT
# excluded: they are ordinary modules, they import no test runner, and a `.dockerignore`
# that guessed at "looks like test code" would break the build for a real import.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.test-d.ts
**/*.probe.ts
vitest.config.mts
vitest.probe.mts

# --------------------------------------------------------- host-side, not container-side
# ⚠ `scripts/hash-password.py` is excluded from the IMAGE and required on the HOST
# (INSTALL-SPEC §11.3). Nothing inside the container ever hashes a password; the producer
# runs on the box, under `dashboard.sh set-password`, and reaches the box by rsync.
scripts
dashboard.sh
systemd
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ------------------------------------------------------------- documents and the pipeline
pipeline
SPEC.md
MOCK.html
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
